# Database migrations (Alembic)

Run these **from the `backend/` directory** with the project virtualenv:

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic check     # fails if models and migrations drifted
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic heads     # must print exactly one head
```

## How the connection is configured

`alembic.ini` deliberately does **not** contain a database URL. `alembic/env.py`
reads `DATABASE_URL` through `app.core.config.settings` (same as the API), so
migrations always target the same database as the running app.

## Rules

- One migration per change, with a descriptive message.
- Never edit a migration that has already been merged.
- If `alembic heads` prints more than one head, create a merge revision with
  `alembic merge heads` before adding new work.
- Tests apply `upgrade head` to `govjobs_test`; CI applies it to a scratch
  database and runs `alembic check` to catch model/migration drift.
